riscv: dts: sophgo: sg2000: milkv-duos: enable USB in host mode

Enable the shared DWC2 USB controller on the Milk-V Duo S and pin it to
host mode. The single USB2 port is routed by the on-board FSUSB30 mux,
which selects the type-A socket whenever the type-C VBUS is absent, so
host-only needs no mux GPIO. The type-A VBUS is driven by the SoC's
USB_VBUS_EN pad (reset-default function), which the USB PHY asserts when
it enters host mode.

Signed-off-by: d622 <300083818+d622-au@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
index ccccccc..ddddddd 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
@@ -64,3 +64,8 @@
 &watchdog0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&usb {
+	dr_mode = "host";
+	status = "okay";
+};
